# --- Promotion determination ---

qa:ATM-QA-AG19-002-promotion
    a qa:PromotionDecision ;
    qa:finding qa:ATM-QA-AG19-002 ;
    qa:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:promoteToBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:rationale """All three worktrees in the named sweep scope (AG.19, AG.20, AG.21) exhibit the identical open defect: the reply-only finalize/plan-build stack in ack/mod.rs survives in full, duplicating send/outcome.rs's canonical plan-build/execute path. Per repeatable-pattern / strict-earliest-to-latest fix-dispatch policy, the fix is dispatched once to the highest (latest) branch with real commits -- feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing -- and closed on lower branches (AG.19, AG.20) via merge-forward, not via separate per-branch fix dispatch. AG.21 is dev-in-progress, matching AG18-QA-002's promotion target; because this finding is entangled with AG18-QA-002 (both round-trip through the same SendResponseEnvelope/RemoteSendDeliveryOutcome::Delivered wiring in ack/mod.rs), both findings must be dispatched together in the same fix assignment on feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing. AG.22-AG.25 are not yet started and are excluded from this sweep; re-sweep required once they carry real commits.""" .
